{title: The Sealed Book}
{subtitle: Daniel 12:4–13}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] |
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [Bmaj7] | [Bmaj7] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
By the [D#m]river I saw two men stand
One on [Bmaj7]this bank, one on the other [C#]side
One asked the [D#m]man in linen
[C#]How long until the [Bmaj7]wonders end
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
A [D#m]time, times, and half a [F#]time
Till the [Bmaj7]holy people's power [C#]breaks
The words are [D#m]closed and sealed [C#]
Until [Bmaj7]the time of the [D#m]end
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I heard but [C#]did not under[D#m]stand
My [Bmaj7]lord, what will be the out[C#]come?
He [D#m]said go your way, Da[C#]niel
The book [Bmaj7]is sealed until the [D#m]end
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bmaj7]A time, times, and half a [F#]time
Till [Bmaj7]the holy people's power [C#]breaks
The words are [D#m]closed and sealed [C#]
Until the [Bmaj7]time of the [D#m]end
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bmaj7]Many shall be purified and [F#]white
[C#]Refined by the fire of [D#m]truth
[Bmaj7]The wicked shall act wicked[F#]ly
[C#]None of them will understand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bmaj7]From the daily sacrifice taken a[D#m]way
The abomi[Bmaj7]nation that causes deso[D#m]lation
One [Bmaj7]thousand two hundred and ninety [D#m]days
Blessed is he [Bmaj7]who [C#]waits to the [D#m]end
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bmaj7]Go [F#]your [C#]way until the [D#m]end
[Bmaj7]You will rest [F#]and rise to your [D#m]lot
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
